      },
      "message": "fix(sim,motion,app): judge turning, rotary and 5-axis ball kinds on a reduced-fidelity model; the collision laws read its excess\n\n#864 tightened the upright mill kinds' gouge laws by a coarse model's\nexcess (its chord error past the importer's promise) and refused every\nother kind outright. The rule is unchanged - a tolerance gives the excess\nback while a positive tolerance is left, the gate refuses by name past\nthat - and now reaches:\n\n- Turning, band kinds: the meridian scan's gouge clause\n  (turning::gouge_tol_on; blade/thread/form `_warnings_excess`), and the\n  composed blade scan that judges a Part's inspection ask at the post.\n- Every turning kind: the meridian rapid, bar-feed and holder margin.\n- Rotary kinds: the radial field law's band and rapid allowances.\n- Turning nose kinds and the multi-axis ball kinds were already judged\n  by the envelope law (f), which #864 tightened; they are taken off the\n  refused list.\n- Collision laws in verify: shank/holder reach (c) and its mid-turn\n  sweep (c3) grow their bands by the excess and shrink the kerf; rapids\n  in stock (d) and its posed reading give the excess back.\n\nThe gate's floor is per kind (the smallest tolerance any of its laws\nholds, a Part's inspection ask included), and an operation is judged\nwith the worse of its source's and its setup stock's excess.\n\nStill refused, for a stated reason: swarf (the flank is proved only in\nthe generator), the cone and engrave rides, probe, the cross drill and\nplasma.\n\nStructure only, for the 400-line law: turning/blade_law.rs and\nturning/thread_law.rs split from revolve.rs and thread.rs,\nverify/excess.rs from verify/types.rs.\n\nRefs #904\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
